# Buster Sword: Bot1's library holds one card, drawn for the turn, so the trigger's draw is from an empty library. The ability goes on
# (CR 608.2): Bot1 casts Hop to It for nothing (it is on the stack), and only when state-based actions are next checked does Bot1
# lose to the empty library (CR 704.5b), ending the game before the spell resolves.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Mox Sapphire
Mox Emerald
Ornithopter
Buster Sword
Hop to It

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Buster Sword.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Buster Sword.Activate(Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Ornithopter > Bot2)
Bot1.Choose(Hop to It)

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 17
Bot1.LostTo = EmptyLibrary
Result = Bot2 won
Stack = Hop to It
